## Third-party notices

This repository's own source is MIT-licensed (above). The prebuilt panel in
`dist/` is a **self-contained** .NET 8 publish, so it *redistributes* runtime
and framework components that remain under **their owners'** terms — the MIT
grant above applies only to this project's own code, never to those:

| Component | Owner / license |
| --- | --- |
| .NET runtime (`coreclr.dll`, `System.*.dll`, …) | .NET Foundation and Contributors — MIT |
| Windows App SDK / WinUI 3 (`Microsoft.UI.Xaml.dll`, `Microsoft.WindowsAppRuntime.dll`, …) | Microsoft — Microsoft Software License Terms |
| `Microsoft.Windows.SDK.NET.dll` | Microsoft — MIT |

Two practical points if you redistribute this project together with `dist/`:

- keep the table above (it satisfies the notice requirement for the MIT-licensed
  components, and flags the non-MIT one);
- the Windows App SDK components are the ones to check against your own use case.
  Building from source (`build.ps1 -Pack`) reproduces the same set.
